# intent spec

# AIDE HANDOFF

Cold-start protocol for agents reorienting on this project. This is a
snapshot of the current architectural intent, the implementation gap
between intent and code, and the pipeline phase that comes next. It is
NOT historical commentary — superseded design decisions are cut, not
annotated.

---

## ⚠ STOP — REVIEW IN PROGRESS (set 2026-04-26, updated 2026-04-26)

The structural-followup cycle from earlier on 2026-04-26 was halted
by the user because of bugs. A review session on the same date made
**partial progress** and surfaced a major architectural decision that
queues a substantial new pipeline cycle. This banner stays until ALL
surfaces are reviewed and signed off AND the queued work has landed.

**Hard rule established this session — encode permanently:**

> The AIDE pipeline is for CODE ONLY. Never for `.claude/agents/`,
> `.claude/commands/`, or `.claude/skills/`. Those are canonical
> agent / command / skill prompts and ARE the contract. Wrapping
> them in `.aide` specs and re-deriving them through the
> spec-writer → strategist → architect → implementor pipeline is
> the inversion that produced the broken cycle. Direct edits only
> on those surfaces.

This rule must be encoded into the orchestrator command
(`.claude/commands/aide.md`) as a permanent guardrail. It applies to
every host project that installs AIDE, not just this repo.

### What this review session resolved

1. **Architect + Auditor agent files reverted.** The cycle's
   "Brain-First Invariant" additions on
   `.claude/agents/aide/aide-architect.md` and
   `.claude/agents/aide/aide-auditor.md` were wrong-headed — they
   forced brain-before-code, which contradicts the architect's
   correct workflow (read existing code first to understand context,
   then consult the playbook before planning). Both files are back
   at HEAD via `git checkout`. The original instructions were
   structurally correct; the underlying behavioral bug (architect
   reading playbook files from disk via `Read` instead of invoking
   the `study-playbook` skill) is something the queued work will
   address indirectly by tightening the skill's path.

2. **`study-playbook` skill architecture clarified — change queued.**
   The user's multi-month-tested skill content has the right
   structure. The bug: backend-specific prose (wikilinks,
   hub-and-spoke navigation, depth-counting example) currently
   lives inside the package-shipped skill, which must be
   backend-agnostic. The fix is the queued work below.

3. **In-progress edits from this session reverted.** Two earlier
   attempts (stripping the skill, absorbing skill prose into the
   playbook hub section of the obsidian template) were rolled back
   via `git checkout`. The pipeline will redo this work properly
   from scratch.

### Major code refactor queued — MUST run through the AIDE pipeline

The architectural decision below has been signed off by the user
and is the contract the next pipeline cycle works from.

**Architectural decision (final, signed off):**

- `brain.aide` body schema gains a fourth marker-bounded section.
  Section order, prose-then-playbook-then-study-playbook-then-research:
  - `<!-- aide-prose-start -->` / `<!-- aide-prose-end -->` (existing —
    basic brain access; teaches that the MCP labeled `brain` is the
    project's brain MCP and the basics of how to use it)
  - `<!-- aide-playbook-start -->` / `<!-- aide-playbook-end -->`
    (existing — coding-playbook hub seed; trims back to pure
    conventions, NO skill prose)
  - **NEW: `<!-- aide-study-playbook-start -->` /
    `<!-- aide-study-playbook-end -->`** — dedicated to the
    backend-specific `study-playbook` navigation prose (Step 1/2/3
    process, Navigation Rules with depth example, `[[wikilink]]`
    semantics, hub tagging, etc. — the multi-month-tested content
    currently in `.claude/skills/study-playbook/SKILL.md`).
  - `<!-- aide-research-start -->` / `<!-- aide-research-end -->`
    (existing)

- Required entry-point artifacts at install time = THREE (was two):
  - `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md` ← from `playbook` section
    (existing). Stays focused on coding conventions: Task Routing
    table, Always Read First, Sections, Contents.
  - **NEW: `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`** ← from
    `study-playbook` section. Holds the navigation rules the skill
    used to ship inline.
  - `research/research.md` ← from `research` section (existing).

- Skill becomes minimal:
  > Call `aide_brain` once. Following the brain access instructions
  > it returns, read `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md` and follow
  > the navigation it describes.

  That's the entire skill body. No process steps, no rules, no
  examples — those move to `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`.

