## Anti-regression invariants future build phases must hold

These are the hard rules from `.aide/intent.aide` outcomes.undesired
plus the cycle-specific additions. The queued work amends some of
them; amendments are noted inline.

- **Body schema is marker-bounded, not heading-bounded.** No code
  path may walk `^## .+$` boundaries to extract any body section.
- **No tolerant matching of marker variants.** Uppercase,
  mixed-case, stray-whitespace, missing-`aide-`-prefix variants
  are ALL rejected as malformed.
- **Bytes outside marker pairs are silently ignored.**
- **No transitional read path for pre-pivot files.**
- **No silent acceptance of marker-layout violations.**
- **Field-name regression class.** No `Hub` suffix on
  `prose`/`playbook`/`research` field names. *Queued amendment:
  add `studyPlaybook` (camelCase, no suffix).*
- **No `hub` token in code or prose surfaces** (with the documented
  carve-outs and the anti-example carve-out, plus the new
  carve-out in intent #15 above for the study-playbook section's
  user-owned bytes).
- **`aide_info`'s outdated flag is not actionable in this repo.**
- **No code path branches on `name`.**
- **No introspection of `mcpServerConfig.args`.**
- **No silent acceptance of deprecated frontmatter fields.**
- **No server-side substitution in any body section.**
- **No silent `.mcp.json` mutation.**
- **No overwrite of files under `.aide/config/`** on subsequent
  `aide_init` / `aide_upgrade` runs.
- **No new frontmatter field whose only consumer is the parser's
  own validation.**
- **No inline TypeScript constants for entry-point artifact
  bytes.** *Queued: applies to the new `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md`
  artifact too — bytes flow from `brain.aide`, not from a
  TypeScript constant.*
- **No CLAUDE.md scaffolding step under any name.**
- **No backend-driver dispatch, no connector registry, no
  matcher-by-shape.**
- **No reading another consumer's owned body section.** *Queued:
  also `tools/brain` must not read `study-playbook`; the skill
  reads `coding-playbook/study-playbook.md` (the on-disk artifact),
  not the brain.aide body section directly.*
- **No hardcoded sync invocation in any skill or command prompt.**
- **No terminal-punt prose on the success path of any broken brain
  state.**
- **No re-call of `aide_info` (or any boot state read) after sync
  completes in the same session.**
- **The AIDE pipeline is for code only.** `.claude/agents/`,
  `.claude/commands/`, and `.claude/skills/` are never pipelined.
  Per-command `.aide` specs are an anti-pattern. (NEW invariant,
  encoded in the orchestrator command as part of the queued work.)

